[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Composer: Dependency Management in PHP"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Composer is a dependency management tool for PHP. It allows you to declare the libraries your project depends on and it will manage (install/update) them for you. It's similar to npm for Node.js or pip for Python."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Why Use Composer?"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automates dependency installation and updates."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Manages versions and dependencies of dependencies (transitive dependencies)."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Simplifies project setup and deployment."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Promotes code reusability and collaboration."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Installation"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Before installing Composer, ensure you have PHP installed on your system. You can download Composer from the official website or use the command line."},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"On Linux/macOS, you can install Composer globally using the following commands:"},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"php -r "copy('https://getcomposer.org/installer', 'composer-setup.php');"
php composer-setup.php
php -r "unlink('composer-setup.php');"
mv composer.phar /usr/local/bin/composer"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"On Windows, you can download and run the Composer installer from the official website: <https://getcomposer.org/download/>"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"After installation, verify it by running 'composer --version' in your terminal."},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Basic Usage"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"The core of Composer is the 'composer.json' file, which describes the dependencies of your project."},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"composer.json"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"Create a 'composer.json' file in your project root directory. Here's a basic example:"},{"order":18,"type":"code","text":"{
  "name": "vendor/project-name",
  "description": "A brief description of your project",
  "type": "project",
  "require": {
    "php": ">=7.4",
    "monolog/monolog": "^2.0"
  },
  "autoload": {
    "psr-4": {
      "YourNamespace\\": "src/"
    }
  }
}"},{"order":19,"type":"paragraph","text":"Explanation:"},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'name': The vendor and project name (e.g., 'acme/my-project')."},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'description': A short description of the project."},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'type': The project type (e.g., 'project', 'library')."},{"order":23,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'require': Lists the project's dependencies and their versions.  '^2.0' means version 2.0 or higher, but less than 3.0."},{"order":24,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'autoload': Configures how Composer should load your project's classes. 'psr-4' is a common autoloading standard."},{"order":25,"type":"subheading","text":"Installing Dependencies"},{"order":26,"type":"paragraph","text":"To install the dependencies defined in 'composer.json', run the following command in your project directory:"},{"order":27,"type":"code","text":"composer install"},{"order":28,"type":"paragraph","text":"This command will:"},{"order":29,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Read the 'composer.json' file."},{"order":30,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Download the specified dependencies into the 'vendor' directory."},{"order":31,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Create a 'composer.lock' file, which records the exact versions of the installed dependencies. This ensures that everyone working on the project uses the same versions."},{"order":32,"type":"subheading","text":"Updating Dependencies"},{"order":33,"type":"paragraph","text":"To update your dependencies to the latest versions that satisfy the version constraints in 'composer.json', run:"},{"order":34,"type":"code","text":"composer update"},{"order":35,"type":"paragraph","text":"This command will:"},{"order":36,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Check for newer versions of the dependencies."},{"order":37,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Update the 'vendor' directory with the new versions."},{"order":38,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Update the 'composer.lock' file to reflect the new versions."},{"order":39,"type":"subheading","text":"Autoloading"},{"order":40,"type":"paragraph","text":"Composer provides an autoloader that simplifies including your project's classes and the classes of your dependencies.  Include the autoloader in your PHP scripts like this:"},{"order":41,"type":"code","text":"require __DIR__ . '/vendor/autoload.php';"},{"order":42,"type":"paragraph","text":"This line will automatically load all classes defined in your project's 'src/' directory (as configured in 'composer.json') and the classes of your installed dependencies."},{"order":43,"type":"subheading","text":"Adding New Dependencies"},{"order":44,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can add a new dependency to your project using the 'require' command:"},{"order":45,"type":"code","text":"composer require vendor/package:version"},{"order":46,"type":"paragraph","text":"For example, to add the 'symfony/http-foundation' package, you can run:"},{"order":47,"type":"code","text":"composer require symfony/http-foundation"},{"order":48,"type":"paragraph","text":"This command will:"},{"order":49,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Add the dependency to your 'composer.json' file."},{"order":50,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Install the dependency and its dependencies."},{"order":51,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Update the 'composer.lock' file."},{"order":52,"type":"subheading","text":"composer.lock"},{"order":53,"type":"paragraph","text":"The 'composer.lock' file is crucial for ensuring consistent dependency versions across different environments (e.g., development, staging, production). It records the exact versions of all installed packages.  Always commit this file to your version control system."},{"order":54,"type":"paragraph","text":"When deploying your application, run 'composer install' (not 'composer update') to install the exact versions specified in 'composer.lock'."},{"order":55,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":56,"type":"paragraph","text":"Composer is an essential tool for modern PHP development. It simplifies dependency management, promotes code reusability, and ensures consistent environments. By understanding the basics of 'composer.json', 'composer install', and 'composer update', you can effectively manage your project's dependencies and streamline your development workflow."}]
